# Project Rules

## Project Shape
- This project is configured for SwarmForge with six Codex-backed agents: specifier, coder, cleaner, architect, hardender, and QA.
- Project language: Babashka.

## Local Configuration
- Preserve project-local SwarmForge configuration under `swarmforge/`.
- Keep swarm state local under `.swarmforge/`, worktrees under `.worktrees/`, and shared scripts under `swarmforge/scripts/`.

## Handoffs
- Prefer terse, explicit handoffs that report state and request role-appropriate review. Do not include verifications or sender process narrative.

## Ownership
- Do not change another role's prompt or workflow ownership without explicit user direction.

## Repository Organization
- This repo is a TCC (MBA thesis). `monografia/` is the LaTeX thesis; `algo-suite/`
  is the uv Python workspace holding the empirical pipeline, one member per
  stage: `algo-core` (shared lib), `algo-download`, `algo-transform`,
  `algo-score`, `algo-backtest`, `algo-analyze`. `PRD.md` (repo root) is the
  product roadmap; `algo-suite/specs.md` is the dated architectural-decision
  log (later entries amend, never overwrite). Each tool's technical contract
  is colocated at `algo-suite/algo-<tool>/SPEC.md`.
- **Where to find planned work:** `algo-suite/docs/stories/00-PLAN.md` is the
  single entry point for what is done, what remains, in what order, and which
  spec file owns each piece — read it first. It links out to the spec map and
  each numbered spec.
- **Story lifecycle:** `algo-suite/docs/stories/{planned,in-progress,done}/`.
  Each story is its own folder (`<NN-short-name>/` while planned/in-progress,
  renamed to `<YYYY-MM-DD>-<short-name>/` once moved to `done/`) containing at
  minimum `spec.md` (the requirements/contract for that slice). A large or
  multi-track spec also gets a `tasks.md` (atomic task breakdown with
  dependencies) — not every story needs one; small stories implement straight
  from `spec.md`. Before implementation starts, the story also gets a
  `progress.md`: a TODO checklist of its deliverables, written up front and
  checked off `[x]` item by item as each is actually completed (code +
  passing test), never marked done in advance of the work.
- **On completion:** move the story folder from `planned/` or `in-progress/`
  into `done/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<short-name>/` and add a `lessons-learned.md`
  alongside its `spec.md` (see existing `done/` folders for the format). Also
  update `00-PLAN.md` §1's state table, the tool's own `SPEC.md` status line,
  and `algo-suite/docs/technical-debt.md` — a spec is not done until the next
  agent can read `00-PLAN.md` alone and see current reality.
